    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "How long have you been experiencing these difficulties with paying attention?",
      "targeted_symptom": "duration",
      "patient_response": "Um, well... I guess it really hasn't been this bad for my whole life or anything. It's mostly just been the last... maybe two years and two months? Give or take? \n\nThat’s, um, that's right around when my wife started working outside the home. So suddenly I had to handle a lot more of the daily schedule on my own, which I was totally happy to do! I really want to pull my weight, you know? I try really hard to be supportive. But... yeah, trying to keep track of all the new schedules and everything on my own, that's when the listening thing got really noticeable. I hope it doesn't sound like I'm just making excuses or complaining about my wife working, because I'm definitely not. Is it normal for things to get a little harder to manage like that when your routine changes?",
