    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "When you notice yourself zoning out or missing what people say, are there specific worries or thoughts running through your mind?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Um, no, not really. I mean, I'm not sitting there worrying about anything specific, like money or... or being anxious or anything like that. I really don't want you to think I'm, like, ignoring them on purpose because I'm stuck in my own head. \n\nIt's more like... my mind just sort of goes blank, or maybe it just hops over to something completely random. Like, I'll be looking right at them, and then suddenly I'm thinking about a piece of machinery at the plant that needs a new belt, or... or wondering if I took the trash out. It's just silly little things, nothing serious. I try so hard to push those thoughts away and focus back on them, I really do. I know I should be paying better attention. Does that sound like a normal thing that happens to people sometimes?",
