    {
      "turn": 4,
      "doctor_question": "Looking back to when you were in elementary or middle school, did you ever have trouble with daydreaming or paying attention in class?",
      "targeted_symptom": "additional_requirement_1",
      "patient_response": "Um, well... I guess I was a little bit of a handful back then, maybe? I mean, I wasn't a bad kid or anything, I promise! I always wanted to do a good job. But, um... yeah, even back in elementary school, my teachers were always having to move my desk around. \n\nI just had a really hard time staying in my seat, you know? I'd get a little antsy. And sometimes I'd get so excited about knowing the answer that I'd just blurt it out before they even called on me. I really didn't mean to be disrespectful, I just... I don't know, it just slipped out. And I guess I got into trouble a few times for kind of hovering over other kids and getting involved in what they were doing instead of my own work. That was all before middle school, mostly. I really tried to be good, though, I swear. Is it pretty common for kids to be a little squirmy and eager like that?",
