      "doctor_question": "Nowadays, do you find yourself feeling physically restless or having trouble sitting still?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S012",
      "patient_response": "Um, well... I guess I do still get a little bit fidgety sometimes. I mean, working at the plant, I'm on my feet and moving around all day, which is great, so it's not usually an issue there! I'm a really hard worker. But, um... yeah, if I *have* to sit still for a while, like if we have a long safety meeting or something, it gets a little tough. \n\nI try my absolute best to just sit quietly and not bother anyone around me, I really do. But... I don't know, it's like this pressure just starts building up inside my chest and my legs. It gets to the point where it feels like I've got to move or do something right that second, or... or I'll just crawl out of my skin. I always try to hide it, though, so I don't look impatient or rude to whoever is talking. I hope that doesn't make me sound like a bad listener or anything. Is it normal for a guy my age to still get that uncomfortable just from having to sit in a chair?",
