      "doctor_question": "Nowadays, do you ever find yourself interrupting people or finishing their sentences before they're done talking?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S016",
      "patient_response": "Um, gosh... I guess I do sometimes. I really try not to, though! I swear I'm not trying to be rude or talk over anyone. I think I just get so eager to help out or answer that I jump the gun a little bit. \n\nLike, um, at work during our shift meetings, the supervisor will be asking a question, and I just sort of... blurt out the answer before he's even finished asking it. Sometimes I'm already halfway through talking before I even realize I didn't let him get to the most important part of what he was trying to say. I always feel terrible right after, and I apologize right away. I just want to show that I'm paying attention and I know my stuff, you know? I really hope he doesn't think I'm trying to be a know-it-all or that I don't respect him. Do you think people understand that sometimes it's just enthusiasm, and not meant to be disrespectful?",
